{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QCodifferentialFormulaProp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QCodifferentialFormulaProp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearMap"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate_not_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate_not_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L282-L290","doc":"Non-degeneracy fails in the degenerate model, so `δq_unique`'s hypothesis\nis doing real work rather than being satisfiable for free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate_adjoint_not_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate_adjoint_not_unique","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L259-L280","doc":"**The old axiom's uniqueness half does not follow from the rest.**\n\nIn the degenerate model every function whatsoever is an adjoint of `d`,\nso over a nontrivial module the adjoint is not unique. The previous\nversion asserted `∃!` with no non-degeneracy hypothesis; this exhibits a\nmodel of everything else in which that `∃!` is false. `δq_unique` above\nis the repaired statement.\n\nScope: this refutes the *unhypothesised* uniqueness claim. It says nothing\nagainst uniqueness on a genuine strictly pseudoconvex CR manifold, where\nthe Webster pairing is non-degenerate and `δq_unique` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.degenerate","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L244-L257","doc":"The degenerate model: identically zero Webster pairing, identity\noperators. All three adjointness conditions hold trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq_unique","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L221-L234","doc":"**Uniqueness of `δ_q`, under the hypothesis it actually needs.**\n\nThe old axiom asserted `∃!` with no non-degeneracy hypothesis. That is\nfalse for a degenerate pairing: the identically zero pairing is bilinear\nand admits *every* function as an adjoint of everything. With right\nnon-degeneracy assumed, uniqueness is a two-line consequence of the\nclosed formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.not_hasAdjoint_of_not_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.not_hasAdjoint_of_not_additive","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L212-L219","doc":"The contrapositive, which is the usable form: a function that the pairing\ndoes **not** see as additive has no adjoint at all. This is what rules out\nthe unrestricted `∀ L, ∃! L_star` of the old axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.additive_of_hasAdjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.additive_of_hasAdjoint","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L201-L210","doc":"**Having an adjoint forces additivity against the pairing.**\n\nIf a bare function `L` admits an adjoint, then `α ↦ ⟨L α, β⟩` is additive\n— not because `L` is, but because the right-hand side `⟨α, L* β⟩` is\nadditive in `α` by bilinearity. So the old axiom, asserting an adjoint for\n*every* function, forces the pairing to see every function as additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_codifferential_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_codifferential_formula","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L177-L187","doc":"**Closed formula for the `q`-codifferential.**\nThe formal adjoint of `d_q` is `δ_q = q⁻¹ δ + (1 - q⁻¹) L_ξ* ∘ ι_ξ`.\n\nThis is the declaration `prop:q-codifferential-formula` resolves to. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-codifferential-formula","label":"prop:q-codifferential-formula","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_codifferential_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_codifferential_exists","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L169-L175","doc":"**Part (a)**: the formal adjoint `δ_q` of `d_q` exists.\n\nThe previous version derived this from `axiom adjoint_exists_unique'`.\nIt is now a consequence of exhibiting `δq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.inner_dq_eq_inner_δq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.inner_dq_eq_inner_δq","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L156-L165","doc":"**Closed formula for the `q`-codifferential.**\n`δ_q = q⁻¹ δ + (1 - q⁻¹) L_ξ* ∘ ι_ξ` is the formal adjoint of `d_q`.\n\nDerived from the three adjointness fields plus bilinearity of the Webster\npairing; nothing here is assumed about `δ_q` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.thetaLie_adjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.thetaLie_adjoint","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L149-L154","doc":"`θ ∧ L_ξ` and `L_ξ* ∘ ι_ξ` are adjoint — the composite of the two\nadjointness fields, and the step the closed formula turns on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq_apply","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L145-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.dq_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.dq_apply","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L141-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δq","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L137-L139","doc":"The `q`-codifferential `δ_q = q⁻¹ δ + (1 - q⁻¹) L_ξ* ∘ ι_ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.dq","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L129-L135","doc":"The `q`-exterior derivative `d_q = q⁻¹ d + (1 - q⁻¹) θ ∧ L_ξ`.\n\nThis was `axiom d_q` plus `axiom d_q_decomposition'` in the previous\nversion: an opaque operator, plus an axiom saying what it equals. It is a\n*definition*, so the decomposition is now `rfl` and both axioms are gone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieStar_adjoint_lie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieStar_adjoint_lie","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L123-L123","doc":"`L_ξ*` is the formal adjoint of `L_ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.iota_adjoint_theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.iota_adjoint_theta","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L121-L121","doc":"`ι_ξ` is the formal adjoint of `θ ∧ (·)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δ_adjoint_d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δ_adjoint_d","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L119-L119","doc":"`δ` is the formal adjoint of `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.thetaWedge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.thetaWedge","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The contact-form wedge `θ ∧ (·)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.iotaReeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.iotaReeb","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The interior product `ι_ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieReebStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieReebStar","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L113-L113","doc":"The adjoint Reeb derivative `L_ξ*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieReeb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.lieReeb","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L111-L111","doc":"The Reeb Lie derivative `L_ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.δ","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L109-L109","doc":"The classical codifferential `δ`, the formal adjoint of `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.d","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L107-L107","doc":"The classical exterior derivative `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.inner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.inner","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L105-L105","doc":"The Webster inner product `⟨·,·⟩_θ`, valued in `R`. Bilinear by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.ContactFormAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L102-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.q_param","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumGeometry.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumGeometry.R_q","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-codifferential-formula-prop.lean#L71-L73","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over `ℤ`).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}